What I Learned
Cisco IOS CLI is used to configure and manage Cisco routers and switches.
The enable command enters privileged EXEC mode.
The configure terminal command enters global configuration mode.
The hostname command changes the device name.
The show commands display device information and configuration.
The exit command leaves the current mode.
The ? symbol provides help with available commands.
The do command allows EXEC commands to be run from configuration modes.

Command                               Purpose
enable                                Enter privileged EXEC mode
configure terminal                    Enter global configuration mode
hostname R1                           Set the device hostname to R1
show running-config                   Display the current running configuration
show ip interface brief               Display interface IP addresses and status
exit                                  Leave the current mode
end                                   Return to privileged EXEC mode
copy running-config startup-config    Save the running configuration

